  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Joining, Leaving, and Replacement Timelines",
    "description": "Track work stage by stage as the active team changes.",
    "teachingApproach": "Treat every team change as a new stage. Compute the work done before the change, carry the remaining fraction forward, then use the new team's rate. Progress from one late joiner to multiple leavers and replacements. The learner should be able to narrate who works in each interval before doing arithmetic.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 31,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 17, Time and Work. Approved scope: Teach piecewise work timelines. Cover one worker starting alone before another joins, all workers starting together before someone leaves, a worker leaving a fixed number of days before completion, one worker being replaced by another, and several workers leaving at different stages. At every stage identify active workers, stage duration, work completed, and remaining work before moving on."
  },
